sdps v4.1 (Vitis 2023.1): shorten MAX_TIMEOUT from 0x1FFFFFFF to 0x1FFFF polls.

The stock value lets a missing or stuck card hang the polled SD driver for
many seconds. The loader runs the machine and the SD service from one loop,
so a long spin freezes the whole shell. Applied to the core-0 BSP only.

Apply from <domain>/bsp/ps7_cortexa9_0/libsrc with: patch -p1
--- a/sdps_v4_1/src/xsdps.h
+++ b/sdps_v4_1/src/xsdps.h
@@ -189,7 +189,7 @@
 
 #define XSDPS_CT_ERROR	0x2L	/**< Command timeout flag */
 #define MAX_TUNING_COUNT	40U		/**< Maximum Tuning count */
-#define MAX_TIMEOUT		0x1FFFFFFFU		/**< Maximum Timeout */
+#define MAX_TIMEOUT 0x1FFFFU
 #define XSDPS_CMD8_VOL_PATTERN	0x1AAU		/**< CMD8 voltage pattern */
 #define XSDPS_RESPOCR_READY	0x80000000U	/**< Ready response */
 #define XSDPS_ACMD41_HCS	0x40000000U	/**< High Capacity Support */
